% 10me Solo pour la Flute, Op. 36 — Henry Altes (Millereau, Paris, 1888).
%
% The whole piece: flute over a piano reduction of the quintet accompaniment,
% 131 bars on three staves, the lower two braced.
%
% Where this came from, and how far to trust it. The notes were read out of a
% MuseScore transcription of the piece and written here by gscore itself, so
% every note, rest, tie, slur, tuplet, accent, dynamic, hairpin, trill, key,
% meter and tempo change in this file came out of that file and has been
% compared back against it note for note. The title, the composer's name and
% the opening tempo are corrected against the original 1888 edition, which is
% the source of truth where the two disagree. Six later tempo marks are the
% transcription's and do not match what the scan appears to say; they are
% listed in the note that came with this file and are left as they were
% rather than guessed at. "Solo." is put back because the original prints it;
% "classic phrasing, vibrato" is taken out because it does not — it is the
% modern transcriber's advice to the player, not Altes's marking.
%
